35,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,The data is clear. Projects succeed when access is shared. Older blocks are traps.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The timetable shows we paid for off-site space for two terms. Specialist rooms sit idle.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The reserve is empty. We bought expensive gear, wrote it off, and forgot to fund replacement.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The tender records show mechanical plant costs rose by a fifth. That’s a huge hidden cost.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The freeze left posts empty, yet technicians still perform manual checks weekly. We are wasting labor.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, shared access is vital, but my data shows the real cost is displaced students.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, I agree. We must stop paying for off-site space. General rooms are full.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, that cost rise is a trap. We are funding new projects with money meant for maintenance.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, exactly. The weather days also show six weeks lost to rain. That’s a schedule killer.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Benjamin, the empty reserve is a symptom. My technicians are exhausted. We need relief.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, compliance is necessary, but not sufficient. My data shows shared access drives satisfaction.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, compliance ignores demand. My data shows general rooms are full while specialist ones sit empty.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, demand is irrelevant if the money doesn’t exist. Option A is a compliance trap.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I hear you. But if we pick something that slips, the weather delays will kill us.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, I agree. We need a plan that doesn’t stretch my team further.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, I respect your need for relief. But Option A’s compliance rationale guarantees on-time delivery.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, compliance ignores the actual shortage. Option B solves the displacement cost I found.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, Option B requires new AV kit. The reserve is empty. We can’t afford the structural rot.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, Option C is outdoor work. The weather data says it’s too risky. Let’s avoid it.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, Option C is outdoor. My team is already drowning. We cannot add more manual labor.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
